•an increase of $28.7 million from our Impact platform primarily due to fees earned from Rise IV following its activation in the first quarter of 2026 and catch-up fees earned from Rise Climate II and Rise Climate TI during the six months ended June 30, 2026;

•an increase of $32.5 million from our Credit platform primarily driven by a higher fee basis across Credit Solutions III, ABC Fund II, ABC Evergreen and MMDL V as a result of new investments. These were partially offset by a reduction in fee basis from MMDL III resulting from the realization of portfolio investments;

